## headscale (juanfont/headscale)

- What: open-source, self-hosted implementation of the Tailscale control
  server (coordination server for a WireGuard mesh network).
- License: BSD-3-Clause.
- Copyright: (c) 2021-2026 Juan Font and the headscale contributors.
  Full license text: https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/blob/main/LICENSE
- How we use it: `scripts/remote-topology/setup.sh` can install headscale
  on the USER'S OWN server and join the Mac + operator nodes to it, so the
  remote-topology coordination plane is self-hosted. We do not vendor or
  modify headscale code; the script downloads the official release binary
  at deploy time.
- Status: integration direction approved for Phase 1; **pending GC final
  ruling** before any public release.

## WebDriverAgent (appium/WebDriverAgent)

- What: Apple's XCTest-based UI automation service running on the iPhone.
- License: BSD-3-Clause (Appium).
- How we use it: `setup.sh` clones the upstream repo and builds it with the
  user's own Apple ID in Xcode. No vendored code.

## WDA signing flow — ideas learned (clean-room)

- The 48h-expiry warning, "re-sign is fully local / never scripts Apple
  credentials", "phone must be unlocked by hand", and "re-signing mid-week
  does not move Apple's 7-day clock" are operational ideas learned from
  ucsandman/SideTap's public docs (signing.py / setup-windows.md).
  No code was copied; `resign.sh` is an independent macOS/Xcode
  implementation of the same operational truths.
